::ENG2_U01_L08_GP_Q01::[MLA.ENG2.R.10; MLA.ENG2.V.01] Passage: The school added a response checklist to the online classroom. The checklist reminded students to paraphrase the passage, include relevant evidence, use precise vocabulary, and check punctuation before submitting work. Question: Which response best paraphrases the passage?{
=A. The checklist helped students review important parts of a short response before submitting it.#Correct. This accurately restates the purpose of the checklist.
~B. The checklist made students write longer answers with more words.#Incorrect. The passage does not focus on length.
~C. The checklist replaced all writing assignments in the online classroom.#Incorrect. The passage does not say the checklist replaced assignments.
~D. The checklist was only about punctuation.#Incorrect. The checklist included several skills, not only punctuation.
}

::ENG2_U01_L08_GP_Q02::[MLA.ENG2.R.10; MLA.ENG2.V.01] Passage: The teacher posted sample responses before students submitted their own work. The samples showed how to answer the question, use evidence, choose precise vocabulary, and write complete sentences. Question: Which academic word best describes "precise vocabulary"?{
~A. confusing#Incorrect. Precise vocabulary should make meaning clearer.
~B. unrelated#Incorrect. Precise vocabulary should fit the topic.
=C. exact#Correct. Precise means exact and clear.
~D. hidden#Incorrect. Precise vocabulary is not hidden.
}

::ENG2_U01_L08_GP_Q03::[MLA.ENG2.R.10; MLA.ENG2.V.01] Passage: The library added a display of student-recommended books. Students used the display to find titles their classmates enjoyed. Question: Which evidence best supports the paraphrase "The display helped students find recommended books"?{
~A. The library had books.#Incorrect. This is too general.
=B. Students used the display to find titles their classmates enjoyed.#Correct. This directly supports the paraphrase.
~C. The display was in the library.#Incorrect. This gives location but not the result.
~D. Students were classmates.#Incorrect. This does not support the paraphrase.
}

::ENG2_U01_L08_GP_Q04::[MLA.ENG2.R.10; MLA.ENG2.V.01] Passage: The school posted bus updates on a screen near the office. Students checked the screen before leaving. Question: Which sentence uses standard English conventions correctly?{
~A. the screen helped students check bus updates before leaving#Incorrect. This needs capitalization and punctuation.
~B. Because students checked the screen before leaving.#Incorrect. This is a fragment.
~C. The screen helped students it had bus updates.#Incorrect. This is a run-on.
=D. The screen helped students check bus updates before leaving.#Correct. This is a complete sentence with correct capitalization and punctuation.
}

::ENG2_U01_L08_GP_Q05::[MLA.ENG2.R.10; MLA.ENG2.V.01] Passage: The response says, "The checklist improved student writing because it reminded students to check evidence, punctuation, and sentence clarity." Question: Which Unit 1 skills are used in this response?{
~A. Only spelling#Incorrect. The response includes more than spelling.
=B. Paraphrase, academic vocabulary, evidence, and conventions#Correct. The response combines the major Unit 1 skills.
~C. Only oral presentation#Incorrect. The response is written and evidence-based.
~D. Unrelated details only#Incorrect. The details are relevant to the response.
}

